WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.717
Is falling perplexity

00:00:01.529 --> 00:00:02.472
just more code

00:00:02.284 --> 00:00:03.003
in training

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.008
OpenAI published a

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:05.538
chart of its

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:06.611
models' perplexity

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:07.590
dropping over time

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:08.970
pitching perplexity

00:00:08.782 --> 00:00:09.866
as a universal

00:00:09.678 --> 00:00:11.187
measure of intelligence

00:00:11.326 --> 00:00:12.552
A footnote reveals

00:00:12.364 --> 00:00:13.259
it was measured

00:00:13.071 --> 00:00:13.873
on a fixed

00:00:13.684 --> 00:00:14.734
corpus of code

00:00:15.262 --> 00:00:16.500
Blogger micjm found

00:00:16.312 --> 00:00:17.125
a paper that

00:00:16.937 --> 00:00:17.962
trained the same

00:00:17.774 --> 00:00:19.967
160 million parameter

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:20.887
model on five

00:00:20.698 --> 00:00:21.629
data mixes

00:00:21.819 --> 00:00:23.103
varying only how

00:00:22.915 --> 00:00:23.882
much was code

00:00:24.398 --> 00:00:26.190
With 75 percent code

00:00:26.261 --> 00:00:27.511
perplexity on code

00:00:27.323 --> 00:00:27.853
fell

00:00:27.948 --> 00:00:29.008
but on non-code

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:29.728
text it rose

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:30.282
sharply

00:00:30.421 --> 00:00:31.187
The point

00:00:31.317 --> 00:00:32.237
the chart needs

00:00:32.048 --> 00:00:33.699
far more qualification

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.244
Full story on

00:00:35.055 --> 00:00:35.951
the dashboard
